  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `posting_plasma.rs`: the plasma clause keeps each warning of the laws as data. The new type is `posting::GateWarning { op, kind, message }`. The kinds are `plasma_tip_up` and `plasma_kerf_crossing`. A refusal stays a gate problem.\n- `posting.rs`: `GateReport` has a new `warnings` field. `verification_report_by` fills it from the plasma clause.\n- `script/api.rs` (`v_verify`): each gate warning goes into the `warnings` row of its operation. It also goes into a new `gate.warnings` list, with the op label. `ok` and `held_by` do not change, because the laws warn and do not refuse.\n- `mcp/job.rs` (`verify`): each gate warning is a finding. The finding has the op label, `move: null`, the kind, the message and `blocks_post: false`.\n- The `not_judged` line does not change. The G-code viewer header shows only this line, so the UI keeps the warnings.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe plasma clause put its warnings into one sentence in `gate.not_judged`. Nothing else carried them. `findings`, the op `warnings` and `ok` read a clean program.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Pin: `mcp_plasma::plasma_mcp_verify_lists_a_tip_up_as_a_finding_and_an_operation_warning`. The test saves a cache with two parts. The rapid into C1 crosses the freed part C0. The test then runs MCP `verify`. It asserts one `plasma_tip_up` finding for `Plasma1` with `blocks_post: false`, the same text in the op `warnings`, no gate problem, an empty `held_by`, and `ok: true`.\n- Red before the fix: yes. On unchanged code, `findings` was `[]` and the warning was only in `not_judged` (`left: 0, right: 1`).\n- Mutations (each run on the pin, then restored):\n  - `mcp/job.rs` back to upstream/main: red (no finding).\n  - The op-row push in `gate_warnings` removed: red (the op warnings assert).\n  - The `GateWarning` push in `plasma_clause` removed: red (no finding).\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` on head `cd3669c58`: 307 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled. This includes `app suites: example_catalog`, `example_catalog_edge_work`, `mcp_plasma` and `plasma_gate`.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Heavy lanes: not run. This is a `P3` PR. AGENTS.md \"Heavy lanes at review\" gives a heavy step only to a `P1` PR.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. I ran `git diff --stat upstream/main -- '*.nc' '*.cl' 'examples/catalog/**'`: no change. The example catalog suites pass. The change does not touch a generator or a post.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The QA project `q06-bracket.camproj` itself. The pin builds the same law result (a rapid over a freed part) on a small fixture.\n- A kerf-crossing warning end to end. It uses the same code path as the tip-up; only the kind name is different.\n- The UI. No UI code changed. The viewer header still reads `not_judged`.\n- A change to the cut order or the rapid route that avoids the freed slugs. That is generator work. It is not in this PR.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #3611 changes `crates/app/src/script/api.rs` (`v_load`, `v_save`). This PR changes `v_verify`. The file is the same; the functions are different. The PR that merges second refreshes.\n- #3251 and #3103 change `crates/app/src/mcp/job.rs` (`list_operation_types`). This PR changes `verify`. The file is the same; the functions are different.\n- #2972, #2974, #2978, #2979, #2981, #2992, #2993 and #2999 change `crates/app/src/posting.rs` (Agie post functions). This PR changes `GateReport` and the end of `verification_report_by`. The file is the same; the functions are different.\n\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/3456-plasma-verify-warnings.md`.\n\nChangelog: verify now lists the plasma laws' tip-up and kerf-crossing warnings as findings (`plasma_tip_up`, `plasma_kerf_crossing`, not blocking) and in the operation's warnings, not only in the gate's not-judged line.\n\nFixes #3456\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
